  "id": "COMPOUND:32416 - PROTEIN:6336",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Tecleanthine may influence Thrombopoietin through a series of molecular interactions. Tecleanthine is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including Methylseleno carboxyethylglutamine, Ginsenoside R10, and Neridienone A, all of which are directed toward Thrombopoietin. This indicates that Tecleanthine may act as a common intermediary in the regulation of Thrombopoietin, possibly through the modulation of downstream targets that influence its expression or activity. The presence of multiple distinct compounds targeting the same downstream pathway suggests a possible role in the regulation of thrombopoietin, potentially through the modulation of signaling pathways or cellular processes that affect its production. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between Tecleanthine and Thrombopoietin, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
